{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"ALSA-2026:103494","published":"2026-11-25T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-11-27T09:00:02.539565920Z","related":["CVE-2026-72061","CVE-2026-72282","CVE-2026-74385","CVE-2026-89450","CVE-2026-90429","CVE-2026-97991","CVE-2026-99462"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-72061","CVE-2026-72282","CVE-2026-74385","CVE-2026-89450","CVE-2026-90429","CVE-2026-97991","CVE-2026-99462"],"summary":"Important: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: net: sit: require CAP_NET_ADMIN in the device netns for changelink (CVE-2026-72061)\n  * kernel: KVM: Move kvm_io_bus_get_dev() locking responsibilities to callers (CVE-2026-72282)\n  * kernel: nvmet-tcp: check return value of nvmet_tcp_set_queue_sock (CVE-2026-74385)\n  * kernel: iommu/tegra241-cmdqv: Reject a vSID wider than the SID_MATCH field (CVE-2026-89450)\n  * kernel: iommu/tegra241-cmdqv: Synchronize the error ISR against VINTF (de)init (CVE-2026-90429)\n  * kernel: vdpa_sim_blk: reject out-of-range sector starts (CVE-2026-97991)\n  * kernel: kernel: Use-after-free via race condition in memory folio truncation (CVE-2026-99462)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * kvm: aarch64 CVE backport CW46 (JIRA:RHEL-305162)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kernel","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/kernel"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.12.0-264.21.1.el10_3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux10/ALSA-2026:103494.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-64k","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/kernel-64k"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","e